/* Verse Games: THE WHOLE COUNSEL · 2 Chronicles chapters 21-25
   Verse text is filled/verified from the KJV by tools/fill-verses.js */
VG.registerBibleChapters("2chronicles", [
{n:21, name:"Jehoram's Judgment", seal:{ref:"2 Chronicles 21:7",verse:"Howbeit the LORD would not destroy the house of David, because of the covenant that he had made with David, and as he promised to give a light to him and to his sons for ever."}, facts:["Did you know Elijah the prophet sent Jehoram a written letter of warning, the only letter of Elijah recorded in Scripture (2 Chronicles 21:12)?","Did you know Jehoram died of the very sickness Elijah foretold, his bowels falling out after two years, and his people made no burning for him as they had for his fathers (2 Chronicles 21:18-19)?","Did you know Scripture closes his life with this cold sentence: he 'departed without being desired,' buried in the city of David but not in the sepulchres of the kings (2 Chronicles 21:20)?"], questions:[
{q:"Who reigned in Jehoshaphat's place when he slept with his fathers?", options:["Jehoram his son","Ahaziah his son","Athaliah his wife","Jehoiada the priest"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 21:1",verse:"Now Jehoshaphat slept with his fathers, and was buried with his fathers in the city of David. And Jehoram his son reigned in his stead.", insight:"The kingdom passed to the son, but a crown is not a character; Jehoram inherited a throne he would waste in eight years."},
{q:"Which of these was NOT named among Jehoram's brethren?", options:["Ahaziah","Azariah","Jehiel","Shephatiah"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 21:2",verse:"And he had brethren the sons of Jehoshaphat, Azariah, and Jehiel, and Zechariah, and Azariah, and Michael, and Shephatiah: all these were the sons of Jehoshaphat king of Israel.", insight:"Azariah, Jehiel, Shephatiah and the rest were sons of Jehoshaphat too, yet only one received the kingdom; blessing is God's to divide, not ours to seize."},
{q:"Why did Jehoshaphat give the kingdom to Jehoram rather than to his brothers?", options:["Because he was the firstborn","Because he was the mightiest in war","Because he had married Athaliah","Because he was the youngest"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 21:3",verse:"And their father gave them great gifts of silver, and of gold, and of precious things, with fenced cities in Judah: but the kingdom gave he to Jehoram; because he was the firstborn.", insight:"The birthright settled the throne, yet birth order never guarantees wisdom; position is given, but a good reign must be earned."},
{q:"What did Jehoshaphat give Jehoram's brothers instead of the kingdom?", options:["Great gifts of silver, gold, precious things, and fenced cities","Horses, chariots, and armories","Lands and vineyards in Edom","The offices of the priesthood"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 21:3",verse:"And their father gave them great gifts of silver, and of gold, and of precious things, with fenced cities in Judah: but the kingdom gave he to Jehoram; because he was the firstborn.", insight:"The father provided for every son generously; it was Jehoram, not his father, who turned plenty into bloodshed."},
{q:"What did Jehoram do once he was strengthened in the kingdom?", options:["He slew all his brethren with the sword","He married the daughter of Ahab","He exiled the princes of Israel","He paid tribute to the Philistines"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 21:4",verse:"Now when Jehoram was risen up to the kingdom of his father, he strengthened himself, and slew all his brethren with the sword, and divers also of the princes of Israel.", insight:"His first act as a strong king was murder; a throne built on brothers' blood can never stand steady."},
{q:"How old was Jehoram when he began to reign, and how long did he reign in Jerusalem?", options:["Thirty and two years old, and he reigned eight years","Twenty and five years old, and he reigned twenty and nine years","Forty years old, and he reigned one year","Thirty years old, and he reigned sixteen years"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 21:5",verse:"Jehoram was thirty and two years old when he began to reign, and he reigned eight years in Jerusalem.", insight:"Eight short years: that was the whole harvest of a reign that began in murder; time flies fastest for those who waste it."},
{q:"Whose daughter did Jehoram take to wife, leading him into the ways of the kings of Israel?", options:["The daughter of Ahab","Jezebel herself","The daughter of Omri","The daughter of Hazael"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 21:6",verse:"And he walked in the way of the kings of Israel, like as did the house of Ahab: for he had the daughter of Ahab to wife: and he wrought that which was evil in the eyes of the LORD.", insight:"He married into Ahab's house and imported its worship with it; whom you join yourself to shapes whom you become."},
{q:"What had the LORD promised David that kept Him from destroying David's house for Jehoram's sake?", options:["To give a light to him and to his sons for ever","An unbroken line of priests for ever","A temple that would never fall","Victory over Edom in every battle"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 21:7",verse:"Howbeit the LORD would not destroy the house of David, because of the covenant that he had made with David, and as he promised to give a light to him and to his sons for ever.", insight:"God kept His promise to David even when David's grandson broke every promise to God; grace to one generation outlasts the sins of the next."},
{q:"Who revolted from under Judah's dominion in Jehoram's days?", options:["The Edomites, and they made themselves a king","The Philistines at Gath","The Ammonites beyond Jordan","The men of Libnah only"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 21:8",verse:"In his days the Edomites revolted from under the dominion of Judah, and made themselves a king.", insight:"Edom threw off the yoke the moment a weak king wore it; kingdoms crack first at the edges when the center rots."},
{q:"How did Jehoram escape the Edomites who had compassed him in?", options:["He rose up by night and smote them","He fled alone to Jerusalem","He paid them a heavy tribute","He hid in the mountains of Judah"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 21:9",verse:"Then Jehoram went forth with his princes, and all his chariots with him: and he rose up by night, and smote the Edomites which compassed him in, and the captains of the chariots.", insight:"One night's victory could not undo a lifetime's folly; God let him win the battle and still lose the kingdom."},
{q:"Which city also revolted from Judah in Jehoram's days?", options:["Libnah","Lachish","Azekah","Gath"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 21:10",verse:"So the Edomites revolted from under the hand of Judah unto this day. The same time also did Libnah revolt from under his hand; because he had forsaken the LORD God of his fathers.", insight:"Libnah followed Edom out the door; when a king forsakes God, even his own cities start looking for the exit."},
{q:"What did Jehoram build in the mountains of Judah?", options:["High places","Fortresses against Edom","Watchtowers for the borders","Altars for burnt offerings to the LORD"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 21:11",verse:"Moreover he made high places in the mountains of Judah, and caused the inhabitants of Jerusalem to commit fornication, and compelled Judah thereto.", insight:"He built worship for idols on Judah's high places; a king's example preaches louder than any priest's sermon."},
{q:"In what form did Elijah's word come to Jehoram?", options:["A writing from Elijah the prophet","A vision in the night","A messenger sent from Samaria","A dream upon his bed"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 21:12",verse:"And there came a writing to him from Elijah the prophet, saying, Thus saith the LORD God of David thy father, Because thou hast not walked in the ways of Jehoshaphat thy father, nor in the ways of Asa king of Judah,", insight:"Elijah wrote instead of coming in person, and the letter outlasted the king; God's warnings reach you even when you would not meet His prophet."},
{q:"What did Elijah's letter say about the brothers Jehoram had slain?", options:["They were better than thyself","They were guilty of treason","They were princes of Judah","They had conspired with Edom"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 21:13",verse:"But hast walked in the way of the kings of Israel, and hast made Judah and the inhabitants of Jerusalem to go a whoring, like to the whoredoms of the house of Ahab, and also hast slain thy brethren of thy father’s house, which were better than thyself:", insight:"The letter called the murdered men better than the murderer; heaven's verdicts do not flatter kings."},
{q:"What great plague did the LORD threaten through Elijah's letter?", options:["A great plague upon his people, his children, his wives, and all his goods","A famine of seven years over Judah","The sword of Syria upon Jerusalem","The captivity of the whole land"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 21:14",verse:"Behold, with a great plague will the LORD smite thy people, and thy children, and thy wives, and all thy goods:", insight:"The judgment was measured out to everything he loved; when a man sows evil, the harvest covers the whole field."},
{q:"What terrible detail did Elijah's letter give about Jehoram's coming sickness?", options:["His bowels would fall out by reason of the sickness day by day","He would be struck blind","His limbs would wither away","He would lose his voice"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 21:15",verse:"And thou shalt have great sickness by disease of thy bowels, until thy bowels fall out by reason of the sickness day by day.", insight:"The prophecy named the disease in dreadful detail, and it came to pass exactly; God's word about judgment is as precise as His word about mercy."},
{q:"Whose spirit did the LORD stir up against Jehoram?", options:["The Philistines, and the Arabians near the Ethiopians","The Syrians of Damascus","The Moabites and Ammonites","The Edomites a second time"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 21:16",verse:"Moreover the LORD stirred up against Jehoram the spirit of the Philistines, and of the Arabians, that were near the Ethiopians:", insight:"God stirred up old enemies against him; those who forget their Defender soon remember their foes."},
{q:"Who was the only son of Jehoram left after the Philistine and Arabian raid?", options:["Jehoahaz, the youngest of his sons","Azariah","Jehiel","Shephatiah"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 21:17",verse:"And they came up into Judah, and brake into it, and carried away all the substance that was found in the king’s house, and his sons also, and his wives; so that there was never a son left him, save Jehoahaz, the youngest of his sons.", insight:"Every other son was carried away, and only the youngest remained; judgment left one lamp burning for David's sake, and no more."},
{q:"What did the people refuse to do for Jehoram at his death?", options:["They made no burning for him, like the burning of his fathers","They would not bury him in the city","They refused to crown his son","They tore down his palace"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 21:19",verse:"And it came to pass, that in process of time, after the end of two years, his bowels fell out by reason of his sickness: so he died of sore diseases. And his people made no burning for him, like the burning of his fathers.", insight:"No fragrant burning honored his burial; a life can be so cold that even its funeral feels empty."},
{q:"How does Scripture sum up the end of Jehoram?", options:["He departed without being desired","He was gathered to his people in honor","He died full of days and riches","He slept in peace with his fathers"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 21:20",verse:"Thirty and two years old was he when he began to reign, and he reigned in Jerusalem eight years, and departed without being desired. Howbeit they buried him in the city of David, but not in the sepulchres of the kings.", insight:"Buried in the city of David but not with the kings, unwanted in death as in life; this is where a Christless reign arrives."}
]},
{n:22, name:"Athaliah's Coup", seal:{ref:"2 Chronicles 22:12",verse:"And he was with them hid in the house of God six years: and Athaliah reigned over the land."}, facts:["Did you know Ahaziah was found hiding in Samaria, brought to Jehu and slain, yet buried only because he was the grandson of Jehoshaphat, who sought the LORD with all his heart (2 Chronicles 22:9)?","Did you know Athaliah, the only woman to seize Judah's throne, murdered all the seed royal of the house of Judah, her own kin (2 Chronicles 22:10)?","Did you know the baby Joash was hidden six years in the house of God by Jehoshabeath, who was both the king's daughter and the priest's wife (2 Chronicles 22:11-12)?"], questions:[
{q:"Whom did the inhabitants of Jerusalem make king after Jehoram?", options:["Ahaziah his youngest son","Athaliah his wife","Jehoiada the priest","An Edomite governor"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 22:1",verse:"And the inhabitants of Jerusalem made Ahaziah his youngest son king in his stead: for the band of men that came with the Arabians to the camp had slain all the eldest. So Ahaziah the son of Jehoram king of Judah reigned.", insight:"The city crowned the youngest because no older son was left; thrones pass on, but the sins of the fathers travel with them."},
{q:"Why was only the youngest son left to take the throne?", options:["The band of men that came with the Arabians had slain all the eldest","Jehoram had slain them all","They had fled to Egypt","They died of the plague"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 22:1",verse:"And the inhabitants of Jerusalem made Ahaziah his youngest son king in his stead: for the band of men that came with the Arabians to the camp had slain all the eldest. So Ahaziah the son of Jehoram king of Judah reigned.", insight:"The raid that fulfilled Elijah's letter emptied the palace of heirs; God's judgments land exactly where He said they would."},
{q:"How old was Ahaziah when he began to reign, and how long did he reign?", options:["Forty and two years old, and he reigned one year","Thirty and two years old, and he reigned eight years","Twenty and five years old, and he reigned twenty nine years","Seven years old, and he reigned forty years"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 22:2",verse:"Forty and two years old was Ahaziah when he began to reign, and he reigned one year in Jerusalem. His mother’s name also was Athaliah the daughter of Omri.", insight:"One year was all he got; a reign built on his mother's counsel ended before it could begin."},
{q:"Who was the mother of Ahaziah?", options:["Athaliah the daughter of Omri","Jezebel the Zidonian","Zibiah of Beersheba","Jehoshabeath the king's daughter"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 22:2",verse:"Forty and two years old was Ahaziah when he began to reign, and he reigned one year in Jerusalem. His mother’s name also was Athaliah the daughter of Omri.", insight:"His mother was Omri's daughter, Ahab's kin; the bloodline of Baal worship ran straight into Judah's palace."},
{q:"Who was Ahaziah's counsellor to do wickedly?", options:["His mother","The priests of the LORD","The elders of Jerusalem","The captains of his guard"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 22:3",verse:"He also walked in the ways of the house of Ahab: for his mother was his counsellor to do wickedly.", insight:"The one voice he trusted most taught him wickedness; be careful whose counsel you call wisdom."},
{q:"In whose ways did Ahaziah walk?", options:["The ways of the house of Ahab","The ways of Jehoshaphat his grandfather","The ways of David his father","The ways of the prophets"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 22:3",verse:"He also walked in the ways of the house of Ahab: for his mother was his counsellor to do wickedly.", insight:"He walked in Ahab's ways because Ahab's house raised him; children usually follow the road their home paves."},
{q:"What did the counsel of the house of Ahab bring upon Ahaziah?", options:["His destruction","Great riches","A long reign","Victory over Syria"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 22:4",verse:"Wherefore he did evil in the sight of the LORD like the house of Ahab: for they were his counsellors after the death of his father to his destruction.", insight:"Scripture says plainly they counselled him to his destruction; not every adviser wants you to survive the advice."},
{q:"Whom did Ahaziah join in war against Hazael king of Syria at Ramothgilead?", options:["Jehoram the son of Ahab king of Israel","Jehu the son of Nimshi","The king of Edom","The Philistines of Gath"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 22:5",verse:"He walked also after their counsel, and went with Jehoram the son of Ahab king of Israel to war against Hazael king of Syria at Ramoth-gilead: and the Syrians smote Joram.", insight:"He marched with Ahab's son to Ahab's old battlefield; the alliances of your family can become the snares of your life."},
{q:"Who smote Joram in that battle?", options:["The Syrians","The Edomites","The Moabites","The Philistines"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 22:5",verse:"He walked also after their counsel, and went with Jehoram the son of Ahab king of Israel to war against Hazael king of Syria at Ramoth-gilead: and the Syrians smote Joram.", insight:"Syria's arrows found the king of Israel; God uses even pagan armies to settle His accounts."},
{q:"Why did Joram return to Jezreel?", options:["To be healed of the wounds they had wounded him with at Ramah","To gather a new army","To hide from Jehu","To crown his son"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 22:6",verse:"And he returned to be healed in Jezreel because of the wounds which were given him at Ramah, when he fought with Hazael king of Syria. And Azariah the son of Jehoram king of Judah went down to see Jehoram the son of Ahab at Jezreel, because he was sick.", insight:"He went to Jezreel for healing and found his grave instead; men plan recoveries, but God plans endings."},
{q:"Why did Ahaziah go down to Jezreel?", options:["To see Jehoram because he was sick","To anoint Jehu king","To make a league with Syria","To flee from Athaliah"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 22:6",verse:"And he returned to be healed in Jezreel because of the wounds which were given him at Ramah, when he fought with Hazael king of Syria. And Azariah the son of Jehoram king of Judah went down to see Jehoram the son of Ahab at Jezreel, because he was sick.", insight:"A friendly visit to a wounded ally walked him straight into God's judgment; some errands are appointments with destiny."},
{q:"How does the chapter explain Ahaziah's fatal visit to Joram?", options:["The destruction of Ahaziah was of God by coming to Joram","He was lured by a false prophet","He sought an alliance with Syria","He fled from his mother's wrath"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 22:7",verse:"And the destruction of Ahaziah was of God by coming to Joram: for when he was come, he went out with Jehoram against Jehu the son of Nimshi, whom the LORD had anointed to cut off the house of Ahab.", insight:"His steps were ordered, though he never knew it; God can turn an ordinary journey into a final reckoning."},
{q:"Whom had the LORD anointed to cut off the house of Ahab?", options:["Jehu the son of Nimshi","Elisha the prophet","Hazael king of Syria","Ahaziah king of Judah"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 22:7",verse:"And the destruction of Ahaziah was of God by coming to Joram: for when he was come, he went out with Jehoram against Jehu the son of Nimshi, whom the LORD had anointed to cut off the house of Ahab.", insight:"God had already chosen Jehu for the work before Ahaziah arrived; heaven's instruments are appointed long before the moment."},
{q:"Whom did Jehu slay when executing judgment upon the house of Ahab?", options:["The princes of Judah, and the sons of the brethren of Ahaziah","The priests of the LORD","The merchants of Samaria","The elders of Jezreel"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 22:8",verse:"And it came to pass, that, when Jehu was executing judgment upon the house of Ahab, and found the princes of Judah, and the sons of the brethren of Ahaziah, that ministered to Ahaziah, he slew them.", insight:"Judah's princes died with Ahab's house because they had joined it; shared sin brings shared judgment."},
{q:"Where was Ahaziah found hiding?", options:["In Samaria","In Jezreel","In Ramothgilead","In the house of God"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 22:9",verse:"And he sought Ahaziah: and they caught him, (for he was hid in Samaria,) and brought him to Jehu: and when they had slain him, they buried him: Because, said they, he is the son of Jehoshaphat, who sought the LORD with all his heart. So the house of Ahaziah had no power to keep still the kingdom.", insight:"He hid in Samaria, the very heart of Ahab's kingdom; the places we run to for safety often become our trap."},
{q:"Why did they bury Ahaziah after Jehu slew him?", options:["Because he was the son of Jehoshaphat, who sought the LORD with all his heart","Because he was the king of Judah","Because Jehu commanded it","Because his mother demanded it"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 22:9",verse:"And he sought Ahaziah: and they caught him, (for he was hid in Samaria,) and brought him to Jehu: and when they had slain him, they buried him: Because, said they, he is the son of Jehoshaphat, who sought the LORD with all his heart. So the house of Ahaziah had no power to keep still the kingdom.", insight:"Only his grandfather's godliness earned him a grave; one man's faith can shelter his children's name long after he is gone."},
{q:"What did Athaliah do when she saw that her son was dead?", options:["She arose and destroyed all the seed royal of the house of Judah","She fled to Samaria","She made peace with Jehu","She crowned herself at once"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 22:10",verse:"But when Athaliah the mother of Ahaziah saw that her son was dead, she arose and destroyed all the seed royal of the house of Judah.", insight:"A grieving mother became a murdering queen; power without God turns even family bonds into kindling."},
{q:"Who rescued the infant Joash from Athaliah's slaughter?", options:["Jehoshabeath, the daughter of the king, the wife of Jehoiada the priest","The queen's nurse acting alone","The captains of the guard","The prophet Elisha"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 22:11",verse:"But Jehoshabeath, the daughter of the king, took Joash the son of Ahaziah, and stole him from among the king’s sons that were slain, and put him and his nurse in a bedchamber. So Jehoshabeath, the daughter of king Jehoram, the wife of Jehoiada the priest, (for she was the sister of Ahaziah,) hid him from Athaliah, so that she slew him not.", insight:"A princess married to a priest risked her life for a baby; God plants His rescuers inside the very palace of the tyrant."},
{q:"Where did Jehoshabeath hide Joash and his nurse?", options:["In a bedchamber","In the temple treasury","In a cave by the Jordan","In Bethlehem"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 22:11",verse:"But Jehoshabeath, the daughter of the king, took Joash the son of Ahaziah, and stole him from among the king’s sons that were slain, and put him and his nurse in a bedchamber. So Jehoshabeath, the daughter of king Jehoram, the wife of Jehoiada the priest, (for she was the sister of Ahaziah,) hid him from Athaliah, so that she slew him not.", insight:"A bedchamber became a sanctuary; God can hide His purposes in the most ordinary rooms."},
{q:"How long was Joash hidden in the house of God, and who reigned meanwhile?", options:["Six years, and Athaliah reigned over the land","Seven years, and Jehu reigned","Three years, and the priests ruled","Twelve years, and no one reigned"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 22:12",verse:"And he was with them hid in the house of God six years: and Athaliah reigned over the land.", insight:"Six years the true king lived in hiding while a usurper ruled; God's promises can wait in the dark without expiring."}
]},
{n:23, name:"Joash Crowned", seal:{ref:"2 Chronicles 23:16",verse:"And Jehoiada made a covenant between him, and between all the people, and between the king, that they should be the LORD’S people."}, facts:["Did you know Jehoiada armed his guards with the very spears, bucklers, and shields that had been king David's, kept in the house of God (2 Chronicles 23:9)?","Did you know the seven-year-old Joash was crowned with the testimony laid upon him, the written law of God placed in his hands at his coronation (2 Chronicles 23:11)?","Did you know Athaliah was seized crying 'Treason, Treason,' and led out to the horse gate to be slain, while the city went quiet and the people rejoiced (2 Chronicles 23:13-21)?"], questions:[
{q:"In which year did Jehoiada the priest move to crown Joash?", options:["In the seventh year","In the third year","In the fortieth year","In the first year"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 23:1",verse:"And in the seventh year Jehoiada strengthened himself, and took the captains of hundreds, Azariah the son of Jeroham, and Ishmael the son of Jehohanan, and Azariah the son of Obed, and Maaseiah the son of Adaiah, and Elishaphat the son of Zichri, into covenant with him.", insight:"He waited until the seventh year, not a day sooner; God's timing is patient, and patience is part of courage."},
{q:"Whom did Jehoiada first take into covenant with him?", options:["The captains of hundreds","The elders of Israel","The prophets of the LORD","The king's bodyguard"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 23:1",verse:"And in the seventh year Jehoiada strengthened himself, and took the captains of hundreds, Azariah the son of Jeroham, and Ishmael the son of Jehohanan, and Azariah the son of Obed, and Maaseiah the son of Adaiah, and Elishaphat the son of Zichri, into covenant with him.", insight:"He began with the captains, not the crowd; a godly plan needs faithful leaders before it needs an audience."},
{q:"Whom did Jehoiada's men gather from all the cities of Judah?", options:["The Levites, and the chief of the fathers of Israel","The mighty men of valor","The merchants and craftsmen","The sons of the prophets"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 23:2",verse:"And they went about in Judah, and gathered the Levites out of all the cities of Judah, and the chief of the fathers of Israel, and they came to Jerusalem.", insight:"They gathered the Levites first, because this was God's work before it was a coup; every true reform starts at the altar."},
{q:"What promise did Jehoiada declare to the congregation in the house of God?", options:["Behold, the king's son shall reign, as the LORD hath said of the sons of David","The LORD will send fire from heaven","Athaliah shall be forgiven","The temple shall be rebuilt"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 23:3",verse:"And all the congregation made a covenant with the king in the house of God. And he said unto them, Behold, the king’s son shall reign, as the LORD hath said of the sons of David.", insight:"He stood on God's promise to David, not on the child's age or the army's strength; covenants outlast usurpers."},
{q:"What duty was given to the third part entering on the sabbath?", options:["To be porters of the doors","To stand at the king's house","To guard the gate of the foundation","To sound the trumpets"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 23:4",verse:"This is the thing that ye shall do; A third part of you entering on the sabbath, of the priests and of the Levites, shall be porters of the doors;", insight:"Porters at the doors: the holiest day needed the humblest guards; no duty is too small when the king's life is at stake."},
{q:"Where was another third part stationed on the coronation day?", options:["At the king's house","At the horse gate","On the walls of Jerusalem","At the Mount of Olives"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 23:5",verse:"And a third part shall be at the king’s house; and a third part at the gate of the foundation: and all the people shall be in the courts of the house of the LORD.", insight:"Every post was assigned, every gate covered; careful planning is not a lack of faith, it is faith with its sleeves rolled up."},
{q:"Who alone were allowed to come into the house of the LORD that day?", options:["The priests, and they that minister of the Levites","The captains of hundreds","All the people of the land","The king's household"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 23:6",verse:"But let none come into the house of the LORD, save the priests, and they that minister of the Levites; they shall go in, for they are holy: but all the people shall keep the watch of the LORD.", insight:"Only the holy might enter, for they were holy; reverence guards the house of God even on a day of triumph."},
{q:"What charge did the Levites receive concerning the young king?", options:["They shall compass the king round about, every man with his weapons in his hand","They shall carry the ark before him","They shall sing without ceasing","They shall offer sacrifices all day"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 23:7",verse:"And the Levites shall compass the king round about, every man with his weapons in his hand; and whosoever else cometh into the house, he shall be put to death: but be ye with the king when he cometh in, and when he goeth out.", insight:"Armed Levites ringed the child king; God protects His anointed, but He expects His people to stand their post."},
{q:"With what weapons did Jehoiada arm the captains of hundreds?", options:["Spears, bucklers, and shields that had been king David's","Swords newly forged in Jerusalem","Bows and slings from the armory","Staves and spears of the guard"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 23:9",verse:"Moreover Jehoiada the priest delivered to the captains of hundreds spears, and bucklers, and shields, that had been king David’s, which were in the house of God.", insight:"David's own weapons, kept in God's house, guarded David's heir; the faith of one generation becomes the shield of the next."},
{q:"What was placed upon the king's son besides the crown?", options:["The testimony","The sword of David","The linen ephod","The royal seal"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 23:11",verse:"Then they brought out the king’s son, and put upon him the crown, and gave him the testimony, and made him king. And Jehoiada and his sons anointed him, and said, God save the king.", insight:"They laid the testimony, God's written law, upon the boy with the crown; a king ruled by Scripture is a king worth crowning."},
{q:"What shout greeted the anointing of young Joash?", options:["God save the king","Long live Joash","Blessed be the LORD","Hosanna in the highest"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 23:11",verse:"Then they brought out the king’s son, and put upon him the crown, and gave him the testimony, and made him king. And Jehoiada and his sons anointed him, and said, God save the king.", insight:"The cry was a prayer, not just a cheer; every good reign begins with God being asked to save the king."},
{q:"What drew Athaliah into the house of the LORD?", options:["The noise of the people running and praising the king","A summons from Jehoiada","The sound of the trumpets of war","A report of a revolt"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 23:12",verse:"Now when Athaliah heard the noise of the people running and praising the king, she came to the people into the house of the LORD:", insight:"She came running toward the sound of joy that was not hers; the triumph of the righteous always exposes the usurper."},
{q:"Where did Athaliah see the young king standing?", options:["At his pillar at the entering in","On the throne of David","By the altar of brass","In the holy place"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 23:13",verse:"And she looked, and, behold, the king stood at his pillar at the entering in, and the princes and the trumpets by the king: and all the people of the land rejoiced, and sounded with trumpets, also the singers with instruments of musick, and such as taught to sing praise. Then Athaliah rent her clothes, and said, Treason, Treason.", insight:"The child stood at the king's pillar, the rightful place; truth does not need to shout to be seen standing."},
{q:"What did Athaliah cry when she saw the crowned king?", options:["Treason, Treason","Mercy, Mercy","Murder, Murder","Save me, Save me"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 23:13",verse:"And she looked, and, behold, the king stood at his pillar at the entering in, and the princes and the trumpets by the king: and all the people of the land rejoiced, and sounded with trumpets, also the singers with instruments of musick, and such as taught to sing praise. Then Athaliah rent her clothes, and said, Treason, Treason.", insight:"She who had murdered the seed royal cried treason; guilt often accuses others of its own crime."},
{q:"Why did Jehoiada order Athaliah to be taken out before she was slain?", options:["Slay her not in the house of the LORD","So the people could stone her","To spare her children","Because she was an anointed queen"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 23:14",verse:"Then Jehoiada the priest brought out the captains of hundreds that were set over the host, and said unto them, Have her forth of the ranges: and whoso followeth her, let him be slain with the sword. For the priest said, Slay her not in the house of the LORD.", insight:"Even in judgment he guarded the holiness of God's house; justice can be firm without being defiled."},
{q:"Where was Athaliah slain?", options:["At the entering of the horse gate by the king's house","In the court of the temple","At the gate of Ephraim","Outside the walls of Jerusalem"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 23:15",verse:"So they laid hands on her; and when she was come to the entering of the horse gate by the king’s house, they slew her there.", insight:"The horse gate, where kings rode out to war, became her end; the proud are often judged at the very place of their pride."},
{q:"What covenant did Jehoiada make that day?", options:["Between him, and all the people, and the king, that they should be the LORD'S people","Between Judah and Israel for ever","Between the priests and the Levites only","Between the king and the captains"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 23:16",verse:"And Jehoiada made a covenant between him, and between all the people, and between the king, that they should be the LORD’S people.", insight:"Priest, people, and king bound themselves to be the LORD's; a nation is healed when all three turn together."},
{q:"What did the people do to the house of Baal?", options:["They brake it down, and slew Mattan the priest of Baal before the altars","They cleansed it and dedicated it to the LORD","They burned it with fire","They sealed its doors for ever"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 23:17",verse:"Then all the people went to the house of Baal, and brake it down, and brake his altars and his images in pieces, and slew Mattan the priest of Baal before the altars.", insight:"They smashed the altars and slew Baal's priest; repentance that leaves the idols standing is only a pause, not a turning."},
{q:"How was the worship of the LORD's house restored?", options:["With burnt offerings, rejoicing, and singing, as David had ordained","With a new altar of brass","With trumpets only, and no singing","By the king offering sacrifices himself"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 23:18",verse:"Also Jehoiada appointed the offices of the house of the LORD by the hand of the priests the Levites, whom David had distributed in the house of the LORD, to offer the burnt offerings of the LORD, as it is written in the law of Moses, with rejoicing and with singing, as it was ordained by David.", insight:"Burnt offerings with rejoicing and singing, as Moses commanded and David ordered; true worship joins obedience with joy."},
{q:"What was the mood of the land after Athaliah was slain?", options:["All the people of the land rejoiced, and the city was quiet","The people mourned for forty days","The city was divided and fearful","The priests fled to the wilderness"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 23:21",verse:"And all the people of the land rejoiced: and the city was quiet, after that they had slain Athaliah with the sword.", insight:"Rejoicing and quiet together: that is what God's justice brings, a deep peace after the tyrant falls."}
]},
{n:24, name:"Zechariah Slain", seal:{ref:"2 Chronicles 24:20",verse:"And the Spirit of God came upon Zechariah the son of Jehoiada the priest, which stood above the people, and said unto them, Thus saith God, Why transgress ye the commandments of the LORD, that ye cannot prosper? because ye have forsaken the LORD, he hath also forsaken you."}, facts:["Did you know a chest set outside the temple gate collected so much money that the king's scribe and the high priest's officer had to empty it day by day (2 Chronicles 24:8-11)?","Did you know Jehoiada the priest, though never a king, was buried in the city of David among the kings, because he had done good toward God and His house (2 Chronicles 24:15-16)?","Did you know Joash had Zechariah stoned in the very court of the house of the LORD, and the dying prophet's last words were, 'The LORD look upon it, and require it' (2 Chronicles 24:21-22)?"], questions:[
{q:"How old was Joash when he began to reign, and how long did he reign?", options:["Seven years old, and he reigned forty years","Eight years old, and he reigned thirty years","Twelve years old, and he reigned twenty years","Twenty years old, and he reigned sixteen years"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 24:1",verse:"Joash was seven years old when he began to reign, and he reigned forty years in Jerusalem. His mother’s name also was Zibiah of Beer-sheba.", insight:"A seven-year-old on the throne for forty years: God can steady a child king when godly hands guide him."},
{q:"What was the secret of Joash's early good reign?", options:["He did right all the days of Jehoiada the priest","His marriage alliances kept him safe","The princes of Judah counselled him","His wealth bought him peace"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 24:2",verse:"And Joash did that which was right in the sight of the LORD all the days of Jehoiada the priest.", insight:"His goodness lasted exactly as long as his mentor lived; borrowed faith never survives the lender's death."},
{q:"How many wives did Jehoiada take for Joash?", options:["Two","One","Three","Seven"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 24:3",verse:"And Jehoiada took for him two wives; and he begat sons and daughters.", insight:"The old priest ordered the young king's household; godly counsel once shaped even the king's family life."},
{q:"What was Joash minded to do after he was established?", options:["To repair the house of the LORD","To build himself a new palace","To make war on Edom","To number the people"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 24:4",verse:"And it came to pass after this, that Joash was minded to repair the house of the LORD.", insight:"His first great purpose was God's house, not his own; the best ambitions of youth are spent on the LORD."},
{q:"What did Joash command the Levites to gather?", options:["Money from all Israel to repair the house of God from year to year","Timber from the forests of Lebanon","Stones from the royal quarries","Volunteers for the army"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 24:5",verse:"And he gathered together the priests and the Levites, and said to them, Go out unto the cities of Judah, and gather of all Israel money to repair the house of your God from year to year, and see that ye hasten the matter. Howbeit the Levites hastened it not.", insight:"He sent them out to every city with a yearly charge; God's work deserves steady giving, not one excited offering."},
{q:"How did the Levites respond to the king's command to hasten the repairs?", options:["They hastened it not","They refused outright","They demanded more silver","They fled to Samaria"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 24:5",verse:"And he gathered together the priests and the Levites, and said to them, Go out unto the cities of Judah, and gather of all Israel money to repair the house of your God from year to year, and see that ye hasten the matter. Howbeit the Levites hastened it not.", insight:"Even Levites can drag their feet on God's work; a command from the king could not supply what their hearts lacked."},
{q:"What had the sons of Athaliah done to the house of God?", options:["They had broken it up, and bestowed its dedicated things upon the Baalim","They had burned it with fire","They had sold its gold to Syria","They had turned it into a palace"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 24:7",verse:"For the sons of Athaliah, that wicked woman, had broken up the house of God; and also all the dedicated things of the house of the LORD did they bestow upon Baalim.", insight:"Athaliah's sons had stripped God's house to dress their idols; what sin steals from God, repentance must restore."},
{q:"What did they make at the king's commandment to receive the offering?", options:["A chest, set without at the gate of the house of the LORD","A new altar of brass","A treasury chamber in the palace","A silver basin for the priests"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 24:8",verse:"And at the king’s commandment they made a chest, and set it without at the gate of the house of the LORD.", insight:"One plain chest at the gate did what royal orders could not; sometimes the simplest vessel carries the greatest giving."},
{q:"How did the people respond to the proclamation?", options:["All the princes and all the people rejoiced, and brought in until they had made an end","They gave grudgingly, under threat","Only the rich brought gifts","They gave once and stopped"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 24:10",verse:"And all the princes and all the people rejoiced, and brought in, and cast into the chest, until they had made an end.", insight:"They rejoiced as they gave, and gave until the work was funded; joyful generosity finishes what it starts."},
{q:"Who emptied the chest, and how often?", options:["The king's scribe and the high priest's officer, day by day","The Levites alone, once a month","The captains of hundreds, weekly","The merchants of Jerusalem, yearly"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 24:11",verse:"Now it came to pass, that at what time the chest was brought unto the king’s office by the hand of the Levites, and when they saw that there was much money, the king’s scribe and the high priest’s officer came and emptied the chest, and took it, and carried it to his place again. Thus they did day by day, and gathered money in abundance.", insight:"Day by day the chest was emptied, because day by day it was filled; faithful giving is a daily habit, not a yearly event."},
{q:"What workmen were hired to repair the house of the LORD?", options:["Masons and carpenters, and such as wrought iron and brass","Goldsmiths and engravers only","Scribes and singers","Soldiers and watchmen"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 24:12",verse:"And the king and Jehoiada gave it to such as did the work of the service of the house of the LORD, and hired masons and carpenters to repair the house of the LORD, and also such as wrought iron and brass to mend the house of the LORD.", insight:"Stone, timber, iron, and brass: every craft has a place in God's house, and no honest work is too low for it."},
{q:"What was made with the rest of the money?", options:["Vessels of gold and silver for the house of the LORD","A palace for the king","Tribute to the king of Syria","Wages for the army"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 24:14",verse:"And when they had finished it, they brought the rest of the money before the king and Jehoiada, whereof were made vessels for the house of the LORD, even vessels to minister, and to offer withal, and spoons, and vessels of gold and silver. And they offered burnt offerings in the house of the LORD continually all the days of Jehoiada.", insight:"The surplus became vessels for ministry, not treasure for the palace; when God's house is first, there is always enough left over."},
{q:"How old was Jehoiada when he died?", options:["An hundred and thirty years old","An hundred and twenty years old","Ninety and nine years old","An hundred and ten years old"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 24:15",verse:"But Jehoiada waxed old, and was full of days when he died; an hundred and thirty years old was he when he died.", insight:"One hundred and thirty years, full of days; a long life spent for God is a long life well spent."},
{q:"What rare honor did the priest Jehoiada receive at his burial?", options:["They buried him in the city of David among the kings","They made a burning for him like the kings","They set up a statue in the temple","They crowned him after death"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 24:16",verse:"And they buried him in the city of David among the kings, because he had done good in Israel, both toward God, and toward his house.", insight:"A priest buried among kings, because he had done good toward God and His house; heaven's honors do not follow earthly titles."},
{q:"What happened after the death of Jehoiada?", options:["The princes of Judah made obeisance to the king, and the king hearkened unto them","The people demanded a new priest","The temple was closed","Joash fled to Samaria"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 24:17",verse:"Now after the death of Jehoiada came the princes of Judah, and made obeisance to the king. Then the king hearkened unto them.", insight:"Flatterers bowed, and the king bent; the moment godly counsel died, ungodly counsel filled the room."},
{q:"What did Joash and the princes do next?", options:["They left the house of the LORD and served groves and idols","They rebuilt the high places","They made a league with Syria","They closed the temple gates"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 24:18",verse:"And they left the house of the LORD God of their fathers, and served groves and idols: and wrath came upon Judah and Jerusalem for this their trespass.", insight:"From repairing God's house to serving idols in one step; a heart without roots falls faster than it ever grew."},
{q:"What warning did Zechariah the son of Jehoiada give the people?", options:["Because ye have forsaken the LORD, he hath also forsaken you","The temple will fall within forty days","Syria will spare the city","The king will live long and prosper"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 24:20",verse:"And the Spirit of God came upon Zechariah the son of Jehoiada the priest, which stood above the people, and said unto them, Thus saith God, Why transgress ye the commandments of the LORD, that ye cannot prosper? because ye have forsaken the LORD, he hath also forsaken you.", insight:"The Spirit of God spoke through the priest's son: forsake the LORD and He will forsake you; the warning was mercy before it was judgment."},
{q:"How was Zechariah killed?", options:["They stoned him with stones at the commandment of the king in the court of the house of the LORD","He was slain with the sword in battle","He was cast into prison and starved","He was burned with fire"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 24:21",verse:"And they conspired against him, and stoned him with stones at the commandment of the king in the court of the house of the LORD.", insight:"Stoned in the temple court by the king he had crowned as a boy; the place of worship became the place of murder."},
{q:"What were Zechariah's dying words?", options:["The LORD look upon it, and require it","Father, forgive them","I commend my spirit to God","The LORD will avenge me speedily"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 24:22",verse:"Thus Joash the king remembered not the kindness which Jehoiada his father had done to him, but slew his son. And when he died, he said, The LORD look upon it, and require it.", insight:"He did not curse his killers; he appealed to heaven. Vengeance belongs to the LORD, and Zechariah left it there."},
{q:"How large was the Syrian army that defeated Judah's great host?", options:["A small company of men","Forty thousand horsemen","A hundred thousand footmen","The whole host of Damascus"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 24:24",verse:"For the army of the Syrians came with a small company of men, and the LORD delivered a very great host into their hand, because they had forsaken the LORD God of their fathers. So they executed judgment against Joash.", insight:"A small company routed a very great host, because the LORD had forsaken them; numbers mean nothing when God steps aside."}
]},
{n:25, name:"Amaziah's Pride", seal:{ref:"2 Chronicles 25:2",verse:"And he did that which was right in the sight of the LORD, but not with a perfect heart."}, facts:["Did you know Amaziah hired 100,000 Israelite mercenaries for 100 talents of silver, then sent them home at a man of God's word, trusting that 'The LORD is able to give thee much more than this' (2 Chronicles 25:6-9)?","Did you know Amaziah worshiped the very gods of the Edomites he had just defeated, gods that 'could not deliver their own people out of thine hand' (2 Chronicles 25:14-15)?","Did you know Joash of Israel answered Amaziah's challenge with the parable of the thistle and the cedar, then broke down 400 cubits of Jerusalem's wall (2 Chronicles 25:18-23)?"], questions:[
{q:"How old was Amaziah when he began to reign?", options:["Twenty and five","Thirty and two","Forty and two","Seven"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 25:1",verse:"Amaziah was twenty and five years old when he began to reign, and he reigned twenty and nine years in Jerusalem. And his mother’s name was Jehoaddan of Jerusalem.", insight:"Twenty-five and full of promise, yet the chapter will show promise is not the same as a perfect heart."},
{q:"What flaw marked Amaziah's reign from the start?", options:["He did right, but not with a perfect heart","He served Baal openly","He never repaired the temple","He refused all counsel"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 25:2",verse:"And he did that which was right in the sight of the LORD, but not with a perfect heart.", insight:"Right deeds with a divided heart: that is the whole tragedy of Amaziah in one sentence, and of many since."},
{q:"What justice did Amaziah carry out, and what mercy did he show with it?", options:["He slew his father's murderers, but spared their children, as Moses commanded","He slew the murderers and all their families","He pardoned the murderers entirely","He exiled them to Edom"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 25:4",verse:"But he slew not their children, but did as it is written in the law in the book of Moses, where the LORD commanded, saying, The fathers shall not die for the children, neither shall the children die for the fathers, but every man shall die for his own sin.", insight:"He obeyed Moses: every man shall die for his own sin; even a flawed king can do one thing exactly right."},
{q:"How many fighting men did Amaziah number from twenty years old and above?", options:["Three hundred thousand choice men","One hundred thousand mighty men","Six hundred thousand footmen","Fifty thousand horsemen"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 25:5",verse:"Moreover Amaziah gathered Judah together, and made them captains over thousands, and captains over hundreds, according to the houses of their fathers, throughout all Judah and Benjamin: and he numbered them from twenty years old and above, and found them three hundred thousand choice men, able to go forth to war, that could handle spear and shield.", insight:"Three hundred thousand spears and shields, yet his greatest victory would come after he sent help away; God is not counting soldiers."},
{q:"How many Israelite mercenaries did Amaziah hire, and for what price?", options:["An hundred thousand mighty men, for an hundred talents of silver","Fifty thousand archers, for fifty talents of gold","Ten thousand horsemen, for ten talents","Three thousand guards, for three talents"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 25:6",verse:"He hired also an hundred thousand mighty men of valour out of Israel for an hundred talents of silver.", insight:"He tried to buy victory with silver; the man of God would soon show him that obedience is cheaper and stronger."},
{q:"What did the man of God forbid Amaziah to do?", options:["Let not the army of Israel go with thee, for the LORD is not with Israel","Do not go up against Edom","Do not number the people","Do not repair the temple"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 25:7",verse:"But there came a man of God to him, saying, O king, let not the army of Israel go with thee; for the LORD is not with Israel, to wit, with all the children of Ephraim.", insight:"God's prophet drew a line around the mercenaries; some helpers look like strength and are really a snare."},
{q:"What did the man of God say about God's power?", options:["God hath power to help, and to cast down","God will only bless Judah","God cannot save without an army","God helps only the strong"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 25:8",verse:"But if thou wilt go, do it, be strong for the battle: God shall make thee fall before the enemy: for God hath power to help, and to cast down.", insight:"Power to help and power to cast down, both in the same hand; the battle belongs to the LORD either way."},
{q:"What answer did the man of God give about the hundred talents already paid?", options:["The LORD is able to give thee much more than this","The silver is lost for ever","Demand it back from Ephraim","Count it as an offering"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 25:9",verse:"And Amaziah said to the man of God, But what shall we do for the hundred talents which I have given to the army of Israel? And the man of God answered, The LORD is able to give thee much more than this.", insight:"Obedience is never a bad bargain; what you lose in following God, He can repay many times over."},
{q:"Where did Amaziah defeat the children of Seir, and how many fell?", options:["In the valley of salt, ten thousand","At Ramothgilead, twenty thousand","By the Jordan, five thousand","On Mount Seir, thirty thousand"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 25:11",verse:"And Amaziah strengthened himself, and led forth his people, and went to the valley of salt, and smote of the children of Seir ten thousand.", insight:"Ten thousand fell in the valley of salt without Israel's help; the victory proved the prophet right."},
{q:"What did the children of Judah do with the other ten thousand Edomite captives?", options:["They cast them down from the top of the rock, that they all brake their pieces","They sold them as slaves","They set them free","They made them pay tribute"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 25:12",verse:"And other ten thousand left alive did the children of Judah carry away captive, and brought them unto the top of the rock, and cast them down from the top of the rock, that they all were broken in pieces.", insight:"Victory curdled into cruelty at the top of the rock; winning a battle can still lose you your soul."},
{q:"What did the dismissed Israelite soldiers do on their way home?", options:["They fell upon the cities of Judah, from Samaria to Bethhoron, and smote three thousand","They joined the Edomites","They marched on Jerusalem","They returned quietly to their homes"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 25:13",verse:"But the soldiers of the army which Amaziah sent back, that they should not go with him to battle, fell upon the cities of Judah, from Samaria even unto Beth-horon, and smote three thousand of them, and took much spoil.", insight:"The hired swords he sent home in anger burned his cities; dismissed help can become a fresh enemy."},
{q:"What did Amaziah bring home from the slaughter of the Edomites?", options:["The gods of the children of Seir, and set them up to be his gods","The gold of their temples for the LORD","Their king as a hostage","Nothing, he left all the spoil"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 25:14",verse:"Now it came to pass, after that Amaziah was come from the slaughter of the Edomites, that he brought the gods of the children of Seir, and set them up to be his gods, and bowed down himself before them, and burned incense unto them.", insight:"He conquered Edom and then bowed to its gods; the strangest defeat is worshiping what you have beaten."},
{q:"What cutting question did the LORD's prophet put to Amaziah?", options:["Why hast thou sought after the gods of the people, which could not deliver their own people out of thine hand","Why didst thou spare the Edomites","Who gave thee the victory","Wherefore didst thou dismiss Israel"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 25:15",verse:"Wherefore the anger of the LORD was kindled against Amaziah, and he sent unto him a prophet, which said unto him, Why hast thou sought after the gods of the people, which could not deliver their own people out of thine hand?", insight:"Why worship gods that could not save their own people? Idolatry never survives one honest question."},
{q:"How did Amaziah answer the prophet's rebuke?", options:["Art thou made of the king's counsel? forbear; why shouldest thou be smitten","Thou speakest truly, I repent","Bring me a sacrifice for my sin","Leave my presence in peace"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 25:16",verse:"And it came to pass, as he talked with him, that the king said unto him, Art thou made of the king’s counsel? forbear; why shouldest thou be smitten? Then the prophet forbare, and said, I know that God hath determined to destroy thee, because thou hast done this, and hast not hearkened unto my counsel.", insight:"He threatened the messenger instead of heeding the message; silencing the prophet never silences the prophecy."},
{q:"What challenge did Amaziah send to Joash king of Israel?", options:["Come, let us see one another in the face","Give me thy daughter to wife","Pay me a hundred talents","Surrender Samaria"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 25:17",verse:"Then Amaziah king of Judah took advice, and sent to Joash, the son of Jehoahaz, the son of Jehu, king of Israel, saying, Come, let us see one another in the face.", insight:"Flushed with victory over Edom, he picked a fight with Israel; pride always looks for a bigger stage."},
{q:"In Joash's parable, what happened to the thistle of Lebanon?", options:["A wild beast passed by and trode down the thistle","The cedar gave it shade","It was planted by the waters","It grew taller than the cedar"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 25:18",verse:"And Joash king of Israel sent to Amaziah king of Judah, saying, The thistle that was in Lebanon sent to the cedar that was in Lebanon, saying, Give thy daughter to my son to wife: and there passed by a wild beast that was in Lebanon, and trode down the thistle.", insight:"Joash called him a thistle challenging a cedar; it is a mercy when God sends a parable before He sends a battle."},
{q:"What warning did Joash give about Amaziah's boasting heart?", options:["Thine heart lifteth thee up to boast: abide now at home","Thy gods will save thee","Come quickly to Samaria","Thy army is too small"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 25:19",verse:"Thou sayest, Lo, thou hast smitten the Edomites; and thine heart lifteth thee up to boast: abide now at home; why shouldest thou meddle to thine hurt, that thou shouldest fall, even thou, and Judah with thee?", insight:"Abide now at home: good advice from an enemy is still good advice, and pride rarely takes it."},
{q:"Why would Amaziah not hear the warning?", options:["For it came of God, that he might deliver them into the hand of their enemies, because they sought after the gods of Edom","Because his captains urged him on","Because he feared his people","Because the prophet had lied"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 25:20",verse:"But Amaziah would not hear; for it came of God, that he might deliver them into the hand of their enemies, because they sought after the gods of Edom.", insight:"God let his stubbornness run its course; when a man will not be warned, his will becomes his judgment."},
{q:"How much of Jerusalem's wall did Joash break down?", options:["Four hundred cubits, from the gate of Ephraim to the corner gate","A thousand cubits","The whole wall round about","Only the gates"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 25:23",verse:"And Joash the king of Israel took Amaziah king of Judah, the son of Joash, the son of Jehoahaz, at Beth-shemesh, and brought him to Jerusalem, and brake down the wall of Jerusalem from the gate of Ephraim to the corner gate, four hundred cubits.", insight:"Four hundred cubits of broken wall measured his pride; the thistle learned what the cedar had warned."},
{q:"How did Amaziah die?", options:["A conspiracy rose in Jerusalem, he fled to Lachish, and they slew him there","He fell in battle at Bethshemesh","He died of a disease in Jerusalem","He was taken captive to Samaria"], a:0, ref:"2 Chronicles 25:27",verse:"Now after the time that Amaziah did turn away from following the LORD they made a conspiracy against him in Jerusalem; and he fled to Lachish: but they sent to Lachish after him, and slew him there.", insight:"He fled to Lachish, but judgment followed him there; there is no city far enough to outrun a forsaken God."}
]}
]);
